● Done. Here's what I did.

  Summary

  I integrated venn_proportional_area as a helper, exactly like scatter, plot,
  bar, etc. — rather than as the standalone sub in your snippet. That means it
  flows through plt and gets all the shared machinery for free (subplots,
  title/xlabel renaming, savefig with Creator metadata, empty-axes cleanup,
  SVG/PNG output, single-plot wrapper calling convention).

  lib/Matplotlib/Simple.pm

  - Added venn_proportional_area to @EXPORT and to the @wrappers list (so the
  exported wrapper is generated the same way as the others).
  - Added venn_proportional_area => \&venn_proportional_area_helper to the
  %dispatch table.
  - Added a %opt entry documenting its accepted per-plot options: alpha,
  key.order, set_colors.
  - Wrote venn_proportional_area_helper($args) following the pie_helper pattern:
  it validates the standard ax/fh/plot args, enforces the 2-or-3-set rule and
  no-undef-values rule from your original, emits from matplotlib_venn import 
  venn2/venn3, defines each set with an ax-scoped variable name (so multiple
  venn subplots don't collide), and draws onto ax$ax with optional
  set_colors/alpha.

  Because it's a helper now, title is handled by the generic plt path (rendered
  as ax.set_title), and output.file replaces your original filename argument.

  Test files — added the matplotlib_venn check

  - t/01.all.tests.t: probes import matplotlib_venn, diags the result, and runs
  a SKIP block that renders a 2-set and a 3-set diagram (validated as SVG) when
  the library is present.
  - t/02.interface.t and t/03.coverage.t: added the same $venn_available probe +
  diag.

  The library is not a hard dependency, so its absence only skips the venn test
  — it never skips the whole file. Verified both ways: 208 tests PASS with
  matplotlib_venn installed (I used an isolated venv), and 01 still PASSes with
  a clean skip when it's absent.

  README.md

  - New ## venn_proportional_area section (placed before ## violin) with the
  install note (pip install matplotlib-venn), an options table, and single- and
  multi-plot examples.
  - Rendered real example images into output.images/single.venn.png and
  output.images/venn.png and referenced them.
  - Mentioned it in the plot-type list near the top with a link to the section.

  One thing worth flagging: a title containing a comma (e.g. 'Three sets, 
  colored') is emitted unquoted and breaks Python — but that's a pre-existing,
  plot-type-agnostic quirk in plot_args (line ~356), not something venn
  introduced, so I left it alone and just avoided a comma in the example. Let me
  know if you'd like me to fix that quoting logic separately.

