● Agent "Claude Code conversation saving" finished · 58s

● Short answer: yes, via a SessionEnd hook — there's no built-in setting for it,
  but Claude Code already keeps every transcript and hooks can copy it into
  your project dir automatically.

  Where your conversations already live

  Claude Code auto-saves every session as JSONL. For this project I verified
  it's at:

  /home/con/.claude/projects/-home-con-Scripts-python-matplotlib-MatPlotLib-Simp
  le/<session-id>.jsonl

  (current session: b3a8edb0-…jsonl). So nothing is lost — the question is just
  getting a copy into the working directory.

  Three options

  1. Manual, readable — /export
  Type /export conversation.txt (or just /export for a menu). This writes a
  human-readable plain-text rendering, not raw JSONL. Best when you occasionally
  want a clean copy.

  2. Automated JSONL copy on session end — SessionEnd hook
  The hook receives transcript_path and cwd, so:

  .claude/settings.local.json (or settings.json):
  {
    "hooks": {
      "SessionEnd": [
        { "hooks": [ { "type": "command",
          "command": "jq -r .transcript_path | xargs -I{} cp {} 
  \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/transcript-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).jsonl\"" } ] }
      ]
    }
  }

  3. Same idea but non-interactive summary — claude -p --resume <session-id> 
  --output-format json "..." if you'd rather generate a digest than dump the raw
  log.

  One caveat for you specifically

  This is a git repo, so dropping transcript-*.jsonl into the cwd will show up
  in git status. If you go with option 2, I'd add transcript-*.jsonl (or a
  conversations/ dir) to .gitignore. You may also prefer exporting to a readable
  .md/.txt over raw JSONL.

  Want me to wire up the SessionEnd hook (into .claude/settings.local.json) plus
  the .gitignore entry? I can use the config skill to do it cleanly — just tell
  me: raw JSONL or a readable format, and into the cwd root or a conversations/
  subdir.

